            <ArticleTitle>Multiple aneurysmatic involvement of sinus of Valsalva.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>627-628</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/echo.13478</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Forty-five-year-old male patient presented with chest pain and dyspnea lasting for three weeks. Transthoracic echocardiography demonstrated a huge right sinus of Valsalva aneurysm. Contrast-enhanced cardiac computed tomography was performed and revealed three large unruptured sinus of Valsalva aneurysms.</AbstractText>
